{"company":{"ticker":"OXY","name":"Occidental Petroleum","sector":"Energy","industry":"E&P","size":"large","cik":797468},"scores":{"growth":52.0,"quality":36.0,"value":71.0,"acceleration":74.0,"price_momentum":58.0,"reality":54.0,"pricing":45.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"OXY","opportunity_score":58.0,"components":{"structural_trend":51.0,"capital_flow":61.0,"acceleration":74.0,"quality":36.0,"valuation":71.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":56.0,"narrative":67.0,"pricing":48.0,"expectations_gap":8.0,"macro_fit":59.0,"sector_rotation":27.0,"theme_pricing":56.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth -20.2% vs -27.3% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +11.2%, FCF margin +24.5%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":false,"evidence":"ROIC +8.6%, incremental ROIC n/a"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +29.5% (+1206 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":false,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 51.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":true,"evidence":"Energy rotation score +27"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":false,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 21.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":true,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 71.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA 0.7"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":false,"evidence":"Diluted share count +1.8% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Occidental Petroleum (OXY) screens at opportunity 58.0 with an expectations gap of 8.0. Reality 56.0 reflects -20.2% TTM revenue growth, +29.5% operating margin and +8.6% ROIC; pricing 48.0 reflects a fair multiple and neutral price momentum. Primary theme exposure: LNG & Energy Security (trend 51.0). Macro fit for Energy in a Goldilocks regime is 59.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 3.1x (93.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 8x (60.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 9.2%","PEG 0.0","12m return +25%, -12% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Revenue growth is accelerating (-20.2% TTM, +7.2 pts) while the multiple has not re-rated.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-08-05)","Continued rotation into Energy"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below -26% (currently -20.2%)","ROIC falls below 5% (currently 8.6%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 29.5%)","Energy rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +27)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","LNG & Energy Security theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":-0.2623,"current":-0.2018},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.0463,"current":0.0863},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.12062816845895591},{"id":"rotation","label":"Energy rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":27.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":8.4},{"id":"theme","label":"LNG & Energy Security theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"lng-energy-security","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":51.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"lng-energy-security","theme":"LNG & Energy Security","weight":0.3,"order":1,"effective":0.3}],"llm":{"thesis":"OXY is an optically cheap, structurally deleveraging E&P where the earnings mix has changed faster than the revenue line suggests: TTM revenue is down 20.2% while operating margin expanded ~1,206bps to 29.5%, net income grew 2.0x, EPS grew 2.8x, and FCF grew 11.2% to a 24.5% FCF margin. That combination \u2014 shrinking top line, exploding bottom line, net debt/EBITDA down to 0.7x \u2014 is far more consistent with portfolio pruning/asset monetization than with demand destruction, and the market appears to be capitalizing the shrinkage rather than the resulting cash engine (7.9x P/E, 4.9x EV/EBITDA, 9.2% FCF yield). The offsetting problem is that this is not a clean 'priced for stagnation' setup: EV/Sales sits at the 93rd percentile and P/FCF at the 83rd percentile of OXY's own 5-year range, so the re-rating has partly happened; the cheapness is sector-relative (71/100), not history-relative (21/100). Add diluted shares +1.8% YoY against only 0.2% buyback yield and the shareholder-return story is currently being consumed by dilution. Net: a moderate-conviction, balance-sheet-quality long in a sector with modest positive rotation (+27) \u2014 sized as a cash-flow/optionality position, not a deep-value re-rating bet.","fundamental_read":"Revenue is still contracting but decelerating in its contraction (-20.2% TTM vs -27.3% prior, +7.2pts of acceleration), while profitability inflected hard: 29.5% operating margin (+1,206bps YoY), 33.7% net margin, $5.3B FCF on $11.0B OCF against $5.7B capex, and 72.7% FCF conversion. The balance sheet is the strongest part of the case \u2014 $9.6B net debt, 0.7x net debt/EBITDA, 6.2x interest coverage, 17.5% ROE \u2014 but ROIC of 8.6% with no incremental ROIC datapoint is mediocre for a capital-intensive E&P and is the quality check the engine failed (quality component 36). Capital returns are the weak link: $117M of buybacks (0.2% yield) versus 1.8% share dilution means net shareholder yield is effectively negative.","technical_read":"Trend is intact but momentum has stalled: price 58.05 sits 8.4% above a rising 200-day (53.56) with a 50>200 uptrend, yet it is below the 20-day (59.86) and essentially at the 50-day (58.31), with RSI 45.7 and negative MACD histogram. That is consolidation after a +13.4% 3-month move, with -0.6% over the last month and still -12.4% from the 52-week high. The 50-day (~58.3) and 200-day (~53.6) are the levels that matter; a close >10% below the 200-day with negative relative strength would invalidate the trend leg of the thesis.","market_expectation":"At 7.9x earnings, 4.9x EV/EBITDA and a 9.2% FCF yield, the market is capitalizing OXY as a terminal-value-impaired, commodity-beta cash cow: no credit for reinvestment (ROIC 8.6%), no credit for the low-carbon/DAC optionality, and an assumption that free cash flow gets absorbed by debt paydown and preferred/dilution rather than reaching common holders. But the percentile data says the market has already paid up versus OXY's own history (EV/Sales 93rd pct, EV/EBITDA 80th pct, P/FCF 83rd pct vs 5y median 2.1x/3.9x/6.0x), so what is actually priced is 'better balance sheet, structurally smaller company' \u2014 a de-risked but lower-growth OXY. The 8-point expectations gap is real but modest; this is not a mispricing of the first order.","what_market_misses":["The revenue decline and the earnings explosion are almost certainly the same event: a divestiture/portfolio-simplification that shrank the top line while raising margin mix and cutting net debt to 0.7x EBITDA. Screens that penalize -20% revenue growth are penalizing a deliberate balance-sheet action (ai_inference).","Operating leverage is arriving faster than the multiple: +1,206bps of margin expansion and +11.2% FCF growth against a P/E that is only at the 60th percentile of its own history \u2014 earnings-based multiples have re-rated far less than sales-based multiples.","A 0.7x net debt/EBITDA with 6.2x interest coverage is unusual balance-sheet capacity for an E&P and creates a dated, under-modeled option on a step-change in buybacks or preferred retirement once deleveraging targets are hit.","Conversely, what the bullish screen misses: cheapness is entirely sector-relative (71/100) and the stock is expensive versus its own 5-year range (21/100 cheapness) \u2014 the 'priced for stagnation' framing is inconsistent with 80th-93rd percentile EV multiples.","Dilution of +1.8% against 0.2% buyback yield means the cash flow is not currently reaching common shareholders; the FCF yield overstates the realized owner yield."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-08-05 filing): confirmation that the margin step-up and ~$5.3B FCF run-rate persist post-portfolio change, not a one-quarter mix artifact.","Capital-return reset \u2014 any announced buyback acceleration or preferred/warrant retirement that turns the 0.2% buyback yield into something approaching the 9.2% FCF yield.","Continued Energy rotation: sector score +27 and the only other positive sector is Technology (+66), with all other sectors deeply negative \u2014 a narrowing rotation set can push flows into energy.","LNG & Energy Security theme (30% weight) re-accelerating from a neutral 51 trend on supply-security headlines.","Reclaim of the 20-day (59.86) with MACD crossing positive would confirm the consolidation resolved higher."],"risks":["Commodity price beta dominates everything: 29.5% operating margins and 9.2% FCF yield are realized-price-dependent and can compress faster than any structural thesis.","Regime probabilities are near-uniform (Goldilocks 26.6, Contraction 25.4, Stagflation 23.5, Reflation 24.6) \u2014 there is no macro edge here; a contraction scenario hits demand while stagflation hits cost inflation on the $5.7B capex base.","ROIC of 8.6% may sit at or below cost of capital; absent incremental ROIC data, reinvestment could be value-neutral, which justifies the market's refusal to pay a growth multiple.","Valuation is at the 93rd percentile on EV/Sales versus its own history \u2014 a smaller revenue base makes sales-based multiples structurally higher, but it removes the 'deep value' cushion.","Continued 1.8% annual dilution outrunning buybacks erodes per-share compounding regardless of aggregate FCF.","Quality component scored 36/100 and theme exposure is not strengthening (trend 51) \u2014 two of the engine's own checks failed."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth deteriorates below -26% (currently -20.2%), indicating the decline is demand/volume-driven rather than divestiture-driven.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 29.5%, signaling the margin step-up was a one-off mix effect.","ROIC falls below 5% (currently 8.6%) or FCF margin drops below ~15% from 24.5%.","Net debt/EBITDA rises back above ~1.5x, removing the balance-sheet optionality that underpins the capital-return case.","Diluted share count grows another >2% with buyback yield still under 1% \u2014 confirms FCF never reaches common holders.","Energy sector rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +27), or adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently 48.9%).","Price closes >10% below the 200-day (53.56) with negative relative strength; LNG & Energy Security theme trend falls below 45."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Oilfield services and completion providers: OXY is spending $5.66B of capex against $11.0B OCF \u2014 sustaining Permian volumes against a declining revenue base requires continued service intensity (pressure pumping, sand, directional drilling, chemicals).","Permian midstream and Gulf Coast takeaway/processing operators: the LNG & Energy Security exposure (30% weight) monetizes through gas gathering, processing and export infrastructure rather than at the E&P wellhead.","Engineering, procurement and construction plus industrial gas/compression suppliers tied to direct air capture and CO2-EOR infrastructure \u2014 OXY's low-carbon ambitions are a capex constraint for OXY and a revenue line for the builders.","Power and gas suppliers to DAC facilities: carbon capture is energy-hungry, making the electricity/gas input provider a structural beneficiary of OXY's decarbonization capex.","Holders of OXY's preferred/warrant structure, who capture the deleveraging benefit ahead of common shareholders \u2014 the same dilution that hurts the equity is a defined return elsewhere in the capital stack (ai_inference)."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue fell 20.2% while operating margin expanded 1,206bps to 29.5% and net income grew 2.0x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Net debt/EBITDA is 0.7x with $9.6B net debt, $4.15B cash and 6.2x interest coverage.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Valuation: 7.9x P/E, 4.9x EV/EBITDA, 3.1x EV/Sales, 9.2% FCF yield; EV/Sales at 93rd percentile and P/FCF at 83rd percentile of the 5-year range.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Diluted shares rose 1.8% YoY while buybacks were only $117M (0.2% yield).","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price 58.05 is above a rising 200-day (53.56) but below the 20-day with RSI 45.7 and negative MACD.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market prices OXY as a low-multiple commodity cash cow with no credit for reinvestment or low-carbon optionality.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The revenue decline is driven by divestiture/portfolio simplification rather than volume or demand loss.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The 0.7x leverage creates capacity for a step-change in buybacks or preferred retirement once deleveraging targets are met.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The engine's 'priced for stagnation' summary is inconsistent with EV multiples sitting at the 80th-93rd percentile of their own history; cheapness is sector-relative only.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Direct air capture and CO2 infrastructure capex transfers value from OXY's equity to EPC, industrial gas and power suppliers.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"A narrowing sector rotation (only Energy +27 and Technology +66 positive) could concentrate incremental flows into large-cap energy.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.48}},"technical":{"score":75,"passes":6,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":true,"stage":"emerging","close":58.05,"sma50":58.31,"sma150":57.02,"sma200":53.56,"sma150_prev4w":55.14,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":49.2,"pct_from_52w_high":-12.4,"rs_6m":-28.7,"rsi14":45.7,"atr20":1.525,"atr_pct":2.63,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-06-30","filed":"2026-08-05","revenue":21671000000.0,"gross_profit":null,"operating_income":6388000000.0,"net_income":7311000000.0,"ebitda":13709000000.0,"ocf":10976000000.0,"capex":566400